fix: iterate all proxy ports for reverse tunnel in full intercept mode

Previously, the VPN service could bind to any of 8081-8084 depending on
port availability, but the backend always set up reverse tunnel for 8081
regardless. This meant traffic from devices where the VPN bound to 8082/8083/8084
had no tunnel to mitmdump.

Changes:
- android_bridge: setup_vpn_proxy() now iterates all proxy ports and uses
  whichever succeeds for the reverse tunnel
- android_bridge: stop_vpn_proxy() cleans up all proxy port reverse tunnels
- android_bridge: is_vpn_running() checks tun0 interface first, dumpsys fallback
- android_bridge: _cleanup_vpn_port() added for clean VPN restart
- mitm_manager: verify mitmdump is actually listening before returning success
- mitm_manager: import socket at module level for health check
- test_mitm_manager: mock socket.create_connection in all tests affected by health check
- NetworkPanel: check result.success before clearing start-vpn pending state
- InspectorVpnService: return bool from startVpn/startLocalProxy, abort VPN if proxy fails
- InspectorVpnService: PROXY_PORTS array with fallback to 8082/8083/8084
- MainActivity: add STOP action intent filter and handler

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>